{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_7xtlcfa424rtwcmktwnwsazooftwjb3jpaks5xqg57rupaic3u6q","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification complete — **the Rust translation is byte-identical to the C for all inputs.** No divergences found, so no fixes to the Rust were needed.\n\n## What the library is\n`c_src` is 13 lines: one exported function `int hdr_compare(const uint8_t *h1, const uint8_t *h2)` plus a `static` helper `hdr_valid`. It's an MPEG-audio frame-header comparator. No options, no structs, no driver binary, no `[features]` in `Cargo.toml`.\n\n## Phase A artifacts (`translation/`)\n| file | content |\n|---|---|\n| `SYMBOLS.md` | 1 C export (`hdr_compare`); Rust exports the same. `hdr_valid` is correctly `static`/unexported in both. |\n| `ERRORS.md` | 11 rows. The C has no error macros/asserts/sentinels — its whole rejection surface is the 5 `hdr_valid` conjuncts + 3 `hdr_compare` conjuncts, all returning `0`. Plus 3 generic FFI-boundary rows. |\n| `CONFIGS.md` | 21 rows over the 12 bit-field axes the C actually branches on (incl. the three *don't-care* axes: `h1[0]`, `h1[1]` bit 0, `h2[2]` bits 1..0). |\n\n## Phase B/C results — 34 tests, all passing\nBoth `.so`s are `dlopen`'d via `libloading`; the Rust is never called directly.\n\nCoverage is effectively **exhaustive**, not just sampled: `hdr_compare` reads only 5 bytes, and rows 17–19 sweep all 65 536 `(h1[1],h2[1])` pairs, all 256×65 536 `(h2[1], h1[2], h2[2])` triples, and all 256 `h2[0]` values — then row 21 hammers the joint 4-byte space with 20 M randomized draws so the factorization those slices rely on is verified rather than assumed.\n\nNotable behaviours confirmed replicated (not \"fixed\"):\n- Only `h2` is validated; `h1` may hold otherwise-invalid fields (e.g. bitrate nibble 15) and still match.\n- `&&` short-circuiting means **`h1` is never dereferenced when `h2` is invalid** — tested with `h1 == NULL` against each of the 5 invalidity causes.\n- No read past `h[2]`, verified with 3-byte-exact heap allocations.\n- Return value is exactly `0`/`1`, never another truthy int.\n\n## Phase D gate\n`run_all.sh` (in the crate root) rebuilds both libraries and runs symbol-parity + the full suite across all 6 configurations (`default` / `--no-default-features` / `--all-features` × debug/release). Symbol diff is **empty** in every one; Rust's only undefined symbols are libc/unwinder imports.\n\nOne environment note: crates.io is blocked by the sandbox proxy, but `libloading 0.8.9` and its deps were already in the local cargo cache, so all cargo commands use `--offline`."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":791,"cache_read_input_tokens":69044,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":791,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"980d76a9-cee7-4db7-8065-6a536993e444","uuid":"a44f5736-d09c-4506-b290-a910fce8eb48","timestamp":"2026-09-05T00:50:20.486Z"}
